     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\left\\{ {\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{x - 3y =  - 8}\\\\\n{ - 3x - y = 4}\n\\end{array}} \\right.\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Test (2, –2).</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"2 - 3\\left( { - 2} \\right) =  - 8\"></span></td>\n<td>Substitute into the first equation.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"2 + 6 =  - 8\"></span></td>\n<td>This is not true. The ordered pair is not a solution to the system because the ordered pair is not a solution to the equation.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "No"
    }
